    {
      "id": "trigonometry-20",
      "title": "Trigonometry: Sine/Cosine Law & Applications",
      "estimatedHours": 7,
      "outcomes": [
        {
          "code": "T1",
          "description": "- Sketch angles in standard position (0°–360°) and identify their reference angles.\n- Determine the quadrant of an angle in standard position and find all angles from 0°–360° that share the same reference angle.\n- Use reflections across the x-axis and/or y-axis to relate any angle from 90°–360° to its reference angle.\n- Draw an angle in standard position given a point P(x, y) on its terminal arm, and identify that P(x, y), P(−x, y), P(−x, −y), and P(x, −y) correspond to angles with the same reference angle.",
          "strand": "Trigonometry"
        },
        {
          "code": "T2",
          "description": "- Solve problems using sine, cosine, and tangent for angles 0°–360° in standard position. [ICT: C6–4.1]",
          "strand": "Trigonometry"
        },
        {
          "code": "T3",
          "description": "- Sketch diagrams to represent problems involving triangles without right angles.\n- Solve non-right triangles using primary trigonometric ratios, the sine law, and the cosine law, including the ambiguous case; use systems of linear equations when needed. [ICT: C6–4.1]\n- Explain the steps in a given proof of the sine law or the cosine law.\n- Determine and explain when a triangle problem has no solution, one solution, or two solutions.",
          "strand": "Trigonometry"
        }
      ],
      "topics": [
        "Review of trigonometric ratios (SOH-CAH-TOA)",
